[finding.1]
file = "services/platform/perps-data/internal/store/facts.go"
line = 1397
class = "restart-recovery"
severity = "high"
observed = "Rebuild and rebuildProject restore orders, positions, market statistics and the perpetual leaderboard but never refold spot_account_legs or spot_leaderboard. Live Project calls FoldSpotBoard. Replay writes through WriteFacts and then Rebuild, so corrected spot trades leave the old realized profit, volume and win-rate rankings persisted and served by projectedRank, including after restart."
expected = "The Project and Rebuild storage interfaces must converge on the same public spot rankings for the same retained facts. Requirements 3492.1 and 3498.1 make these tables the production leaderboard source; recovery must include them, not only the older projection set."
proposal = "In services/platform/perps-data/internal/store/facts.go and spotboard.go, refold affected spot accounts from all surviving history and rerank all three boards in the recovery transaction, including accounts whose last trade was removed. Add real replay and reopen equivalence coverage through the leaderboard HTTP route."
owner_domain = 3
interface = "3.go-perps-data-store-rebuild-j27"

[finding.2]
file = "services/platform/perps-data/internal/store/facts.go"
line = 1431
class = "restart-recovery"
severity = "high"
observed = "Rebuild derives its affected accounts and markets only from facts still present in [from,to], then returns when min(time) in that range is null. The production indexer.rebuild passes a.From as both bounds after source.Follower has deleted blocks at and above that height, discarding source.Affected.Accounts, Markets and FromTime. The call therefore returns without rebuilding the projections the rewind just deleted; older surviving positions and balances remain absent. Replay likewise cannot clean a key appearing only in removed facts."
expected = "A recovery consumer must preserve the affected keys collected before deletion and restore their projections from surviving facts. Requirement 3502.1 requires the rebuilt account to equal a fresh fold, while source.FollowerOptions.Rebuild explicitly supplies discarded accounts and markets for this purpose."
proposal = "Change the recovery interface in services/platform/perps-data/internal/store/facts.go and its internal/indexer/indexer.go and internal/replay/replay.go callers to carry the union of old and replacement keys plus the recovery time. Fold through the surviving head even when the deleted range is empty, remove keys with no history, and prove a rewind of a previously modified position restores its pre-fork state after reopening."
owner_domain = 3
interface = "3.go-perps-data-store-rebuild-j27"

[finding.3]
file = "services/platform/perps-data/internal/replay/replay.go"
line = 53
class = "runtime-risk"
severity = "medium"
observed = "projectionTables omits spot_account_legs and spot_leaderboard. snapshot, projectionQuery and diff consequently exclude both production spot projections, so a dry-run report can show no projection differences while the public spot rankings disagree with the rewritten facts."
expected = "The replay report and dry-run contract in data-services section 7 must account for all projections served to users, including the persisted spot boards introduced by requirements 3484.1, 3492.1 and 3498.1."
proposal = "Extend services/platform/perps-data/internal/replay/replay.go to snapshot and compare affected spot account legs and the globally ranked board, including ranks changed for otherwise untouched accounts. Define their explicit query scopes and assert corrected and removed spot trades appear in the dry-run report without persisting writes."
owner_domain = 3
interface = "3.go-perps-data-replay-report-j27"

[finding.4]
file = "services/platform/perps-data/internal/replay/replay_test.go"
line = 214
class = "test-gap"
severity = "medium"
observed = "The replay test dump and expected snapshot inventory iterate the production projectionTables list, which omits both persisted spot-board tables. The follower test callback at line 124 also passes only the already-deleted fork height into Rebuild. These checks can agree with the same incomplete recovery implementation without observing missing spot rankings or restoration of surviving account history."
expected = "Recovery tests must compare the complete public projection surface independently of the production enumeration and exercise deletion before rebuilding. Brief check 7 requires the real persisted producer-to-consumer path, including recovery."
proposal = "In services/platform/perps-data/internal/replay/replay_test.go, declare an independent expected projection inventory and drive actual WriteBlock, replay and follower recovery with spot trades and a position modified after its opening block. Compare all board values and surviving positions through real readers after closing and reopening the database connection; retain all existing assertions."
owner_domain = 3

[finding.5]
file = "services/platform/perps-data/internal/store/facts_test.go"
line = 196
class = "test-gap"
severity = "medium"
observed = "TestRebuildScoped obtains its fresh-fold baseline by clearing rebuildTables and calling the lower-level project function, followed by perpetual leaderboard rebuilding. Both omit FoldSpotBoard, so this baseline does not represent the public Project path and cannot expose the missing spot recovery. The changed range still contains the affected facts in the tested cases."
expected = "The fresh-fold comparison for requirement 3502.1 must represent the real WriteBlock and Project producer, including every persistent projection and keys removed by a rewrite."
proposal = "Extend services/platform/perps-data/internal/store/facts_test.go with a complete independent projection inventory and a fresh database populated through WriteBlock. Compare spot legs and all three spot boards as well as existing projections, and cover removal of the last fact for an account while preserving untouched-account byte identity."
owner_domain = 3

[finding.6]
file = "services/platform/perps-data/internal/rest/markets.go"
line = 144
class = "runtime-risk"
severity = "medium"
observed = "marketRecordsSQL reads index_price and its timestamp only from mark_prices. records.latestMarkSQL also considers successful index_prices aggregates because a changing index need not change the mark. Consequently GET /api/markets and the portal can publish an older index and basis than the symbol REST route and markets WebSocket provider for the same database head."
expected = "The market record must represent the latest successful index aggregate alongside the latest mark, with consistent values across the REST and WebSocket forms of the market surface. records.go lines 176-198 and the index_only_update case in rest/symbol_test.go establish the producer behavior."
proposal = "In services/platform/perps-data/internal/rest/markets.go, share the successful latest-index selection used by records.Symbol instead of relying on a MarkPriceUpdated event. Preserve exact funding strings and add a cross-route comparison with an index-only update followed by an aggregate_skipped event."
owner_domain = 3
interface = "3.go-perps-data-rest-markets-register-j27"

[finding.7]
file = "services/platform/perps-data/internal/graphql/perps.go"
line = 1115
class = "runtime-risk"
severity = "medium"
observed = "marketStateSQL, latestMarkSQL, OrderlyTickers and OrderlyPriceChanges use mark_prices as the only index-price source. When pricefeed emits an updated index without a changed mark, the GraphQL latest-price, market and ticker surfaces lag records.Symbol and the symbol REST/WebSocket consumers, which merge successful aggregate rows."
expected = "A latest index price must follow the latest successful producer update even when no new mark-price event is emitted. Public readers of the same market should agree on the value, observation time and basis, while mark-price history retains its own event semantics."
proposal = "Consolidate latest index selection in services/platform/perps-data/internal/graphql/perps.go with the records reader, retaining the separate mark value and excluding skipped aggregates. Add real stored producer events and compare GraphQL latestPrices, Market.latestPrice, Orderly tickers and corresponding REST/socket snapshots; update the live data-services contract with the chosen common semantics."
owner_domain = 3
interface = "3.go-perps-data-graphql-newschema-j27"

[finding.8]
file = "services/platform/perps-data/internal/store/projections.go"
line = 766
class = "runtime-risk"
severity = "medium"
observed = "staleMarketStatsSQL refreshes an idle market only when the time of updated_block is more than 24 hours old. With fills at t0 and t0+1h, the first fill expires from volume_24h at t0+24h while updated_block is still less than 24 hours old. Volume, high, low and open retain that expired fill until the later refresh; 7d and 30d changes can also wait for this daily refresh."
expected = "The rolling statistics consumed by market records must describe their stated windows at the current indexed block time, including partial expiry while newer fills remain. Requirement 3487.1 supplies the empty-block expiry case but does not authorize retaining partially expired volume."
proposal = "In services/platform/perps-data/internal/store/projections.go, select markets whose next contributing fill crosses any rolling-window boundary, or maintain equivalent persisted expiry markers. Recompute those markets on empty blocks and prove staggered fills crossing 24h, 7d and 30d boundaries agree with a fresh fold."
owner_domain = 3
interface = "3.go-perps-data-store-project-j27"

[finding.9]
file = "services/platform/perps-data/internal/store/projections.go"
line = 114
class = "runtime-risk"
severity = "medium"
observed = "expiredLeaderboardAccounts chooses an account only when no close and no settlement remain inside a 7d or 30d window. An idle account with an old profitable close and a newer settlement is not refolded when only that close expires, so its realized profit, win rate and rank remain inflated while a newer contribution still exists."
expected = "The 7d and 30d leaderboard values and ranks must remove each expired contribution at the current block time, not only delete an account after its final contribution ages out. Requirement 3503.1 expects equivalence with the full leaderboard rebuild."
proposal = "Update services/platform/perps-data/internal/store/projections.go to track or select accounts at every partial close or settlement expiry and rerank each affected window. Prove an idle account with staggered closes and settlements matches pnl.Leaderboard.Rebuild field for field at each expiry."
owner_domain = 3
interface = "3.go-perps-data-store-project-j27"

[finding.10]
file = "services/platform/perps-data/internal/store/projections_test.go"
line = 1033
class = "test-gap"
severity = "medium"
observed = "TestLeaderboardWindowAgesOut checks only whether an account row exists, so its refreshed case misses stale profit and volume while a newer row remains. TestMarketStatsWindowExpiry at line 720 seeds only one fill and checks 23h and 25h, leaving partial rolling-window expiry unasserted."
expected = "The incremental projection tests must establish metric and rank equivalence with an independent full fold at intermediate window boundaries as required by 3503.1 and the rolling-window contract, not merely final row removal."
proposal = "Extend services/platform/perps-data/internal/store/projections_test.go with staggered fills, positive and negative closes and settlements, then empty blocks just before and at every expiry. Compare every metric and rank with full folds, including accounts retaining newer activity; keep the current zero-volume and row-existence checks."
owner_domain = 3

[finding.11]
file = "services/platform/perps-data/internal/rest/spotusers.go"
line = 1287
class = "interface-mismatch"
severity = "medium"
observed = "projectedRank explicitly has no projection fold timestamp or omission count, assigns as_of from time.Now and leaves omitted_accounts at zero. FoldSpotBoard can omit an account after a PNL attribution refusal, and an indexer outage leaves older ranks persisted, but the HTTP response presents the board as newly folded and complete."
expected = "The GET /v1/leaderboards/{kind} contract in data-services section 25 defines as_of as the time of the fold and omitted_accounts as the number of refused accounts. Switching to the persisted projection under 3498.1 must retain truthful freshness and completeness metadata."
proposal = "Persist board generation time and durable omission state alongside the rankings in services/platform/perps-data/internal/store/spotboard.go and a migration, and read them atomically in internal/rest/spotusers.go. Return the stored metadata through the existing fields and prove it survives an indexer pause and database reopen without a request-time fold."
owner_domain = 3
interface = "3.http-perps-data-rest-get-v1-leaderboards-kind-j27"

[finding.12]
file = "services/platform/perps-data/internal/rest/spotusers.go"
line = 1270
class = "interface-mismatch"
severity = "medium"
observed = "The leaderboard handler returns HTTP 400 for an unknown kind. The declared section-25 route says unknown kind is 404, and TestSpotUsersREST/unknown_kind_404 asserts that status, while TestSpotLeaderboardProjection and ProofRESTSpotUsers assert 400 for the same live route."
expected = "An unsupported leaderboard kind must produce the single declared HTTP 404 refusal consistently through the registered route and every consumer test; malformed limit remains a distinct HTTP 400 input error."
proposal = "Restore the declared unknown-kind 404 behavior in services/platform/perps-data/internal/rest/spotusers.go and reconcile the conflicting tests against that contract while retaining explicit malformed-limit and unknown-kind assertions. Prove the registered mux returns the same error shape and status for both unsupported-kind examples."
owner_domain = 3
interface = "3.http-perps-data-rest-get-v1-leaderboards-kind-j27"

[finding.13]
file = "services/platform/perps-data/internal/rest/spotusers_test.go"
line = 239
class = "test-gap"
severity = "medium"
observed = "TestSpotLeaderboardProjection inserts ranking rows directly and accepts request-time as_of and zero omissions. TestSpotUsersREST seeds only raw spot facts then expects request-time folding, nonzero omissions, a 30-second in-memory cache and unknown-kind 404; its later concurrency case calls the otherwise unused rank method directly. ProofRESTSpotUsers instead expects unknown-kind 400. These paths cannot all describe the registered projectedRank producer."
expected = "Requirement 3498.1 requires reading persisted spot boards without folding at request time, while the public metadata and refusal contract must remain asserted. A real path test must start from the production writer and pass through the registered handler."
proposal = "Rework services/platform/perps-data/internal/rest/spotusers_test.go to populate facts and projections through real WriteBlock and FoldSpotBoard, reopen the store and call the actual mux. Retain omission, freshness, exact-value, bounded-read and error assertions against the declared contract; migrate cache-specific tests to generation consistency without deleting their behavioral protections."
owner_domain = 3

[finding.14]
file = "services/platform/perps-data/internal/config/config.go"
line = 215
class = "security"
severity = "medium"
observed = "Config.String redacts DatabaseURL, NATSURL and AuthSecret but prints RPCURLs, CometURLs, GatewayURL and ExplorerTxBase verbatim. validURL accepts URL userinfo and query values. All service commands log this Config at startup, and GoString, LogValue and default JSON encoding expose the same endpoint strings, allowing endpoint passwords or access tokens into logs."
expected = "Brief check 8 requires secrets never to be logged. Configured service endpoints can carry credentials, and redaction must cover every supported representation rather than only the three explicitly tagged fields."
proposal = "In services/platform/perps-data/internal/config/config.go, centralize safe endpoint rendering that removes userinfo and secret query values for String, GoString, LogValue and JSON, or refuse credential-bearing URLs where unsupported. Extend config_test.go with credential-bearing RPC, Comet and gateway URLs and assert no secret survives any logged representation."
owner_domain = 3
interface = "3.go-perps-data-config-config-string-j27"

[finding.15]
file = "services/platform/perps-data/internal/config/config.go"
line = 171
class = "config-drift"
severity = "medium"
observed = "Validate accepts every nonzero PERPS_CHAIN_ID, but store/facts.go fixes event IDs, delivery envelopes and every fact subject to chainID 125. The indexer publisher policy and gateway subscriptions use cfg.ChainID, so an otherwise accepted value such as 126 makes the writer publish a different namespace from the configured transport and consumer."
expected = "The merged mainnet has EVM chain id 125, and the configuration contract says PERPS_CHAIN_ID is used in every subject. Startup must reject a chain the actual writer cannot serve rather than accept a disconnected message pipeline."
proposal = "Make services/platform/perps-data/internal/config/config.go reject unsupported chain IDs with a clear PERPS_CHAIN_ID error for the current single-network writer. If another chain is intentionally supported later, thread that identity through store.WriteFacts, event IDs, publication policy and gateway consumers in one owning-domain task and prove an actual end-to-end delivery."
owner_domain = 3
interface = "3.env-perps-data-perps-chain-id-j27"

[finding.16]
file = "services/platform/perps-data/internal/config/config.go"
line = 203
class = "config-drift"
severity = "medium"
observed = "The shared GatewayURL validation accepts ws and wss for both portal and loadtest. cmd/perps-portal passes the value unchanged into portal.NewPages, which requires http or https and constructs REST and GraphQL requests. Thus a portal configuration accepted by Load, including the one in config_test.go, fails at the next startup boundary."
expected = "Config.Load is declared to return a validated environment the named service can run with. The portal consumes an HTTP gateway origin; only the loadtest socket path may accept a WebSocket URL."
proposal = "Use service-specific gateway scheme validation in services/platform/perps-data/internal/config/config.go: require http or https for Portal, retain explicitly supported socket forms for Loadtest, and add a real Config-to-NewPages construction case for every accepted portal configuration."
owner_domain = 3
interface = "3.go-perps-data-config-load-j27"

[finding.17]
file = "services/platform/perps-data/internal/portal/pages.go"
line = 142
class = "config-drift"
severity = "medium"
observed = "NewPages validates explorerTxBase with the same nonempty HTTP-origin check as gatewayURL. Config.Validate permits an empty PERPS_EXPLORER_TX_BASE and the configuration contract calls it optional for portal, so omitting optional explorer links prevents the entire portal from starting."
expected = "An optional transaction-link base must be allowed to remain empty while the portal still renders markets and accounts. The explorer already treats the absence as an instruction to omit links."
proposal = "In services/platform/perps-data/internal/portal/pages.go and templates/pages.html, accept an empty explorer base and render transaction hashes without a link in that case. Preserve strict validation of nonempty bases and prove portal construction and account rendering from Config.Load with the optional variable unset."
owner_domain = 3
interface = "3.go-perps-data-portal-newpages-j27"

[finding.18]
file = "services/platform/perps-data/internal/config/config_test.go"
line = 111
class = "test-gap"
severity = "medium"
observed = "The loads_all portal case sets PERPS_GATEWAY_URL to wss://gateway.example/ws and expects success, but portal.NewPages only accepts HTTP or HTTPS and the real portal command directly passes the Config value to it. The test verifies a configuration shape the next production consumer refuses."
